-- title:
--   Automorphisms fixing π permute the minimal primes of (π)
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring, let $\gamma : S \simeq S$ be a ring automorphism of $S$, and let $\pi \in S$ satisfy $\gamma(\pi) = \pi$. Let $P$ be an ideal of $S$ belonging to `(Ideal.span {π}).minimalPrimes`, that is, $P$ is minimal among the prime ideals of $S$ containing the principal ideal $(\pi)$ (in Mathlib's formulation: $P$ is prime and contains $\mathrm{span}\{\pi\}$, and any ideal that is prime, contains $\mathrm{span}\{\pi\}$ and is contained in $P$ equals, indeed contains, $P$). The conclusion is that the image ideal $\gamma(P) = P.\mathrm{map}\,\gamma$, the ideal of $S$ generated by $\{\gamma(x) : x \in P\}$, again lies in `(Ideal.span {π}).minimalPrimes`. In other words, the automorphism $\gamma$ maps the set of minimal primes over $\pi$ into itself; since the same applies to $\gamma^{-1}$, it permutes that set.
--
--   An elementary remark of commutative algebra: a ring automorphism fixing an element $\pi$ preserves the principal ideal $(\pi)$, hence acts on the primes containing it and, inclusions being preserved, on the minimal ones. It is used in the analysis of a crossing model for a modular curve, where the Galois group of an unramified extension of the coefficient ring fixes the thickness parameter and therefore permutes the branches through the crossing point, in [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isUnit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isUnit).
